      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While dermatitis can be an allergic reaction, the symptoms you described, such as warmth, spreading redness, and itching, are more suggestive of an infection. Monitoring yourself is not recommended, and applying over-the-counter cream or ointment without a proper diagnosis can hinder a proper treatment plan. If you do try to monitor it, pay attention to changes in size, color, or drainage (if it starts oozing or becoming crusty), as these could indicate signs of worsening infection.",
